James sought guidance on best practices for imputing R² values in a meta-analysis after receiving reviewer feedback concerning the methodological challenges. I advised using similar models for imputation, multiple imputation techniques, conducting sensitivity analyses, and validating with known data. James then inquired about reporting the success of a cross-validation exercise where known R² values were iteratively dropped and imputed. I suggested detailing the process, using metrics such as Mean Absolute Error (MAE) and correlation coefficients for evaluation, and presenting results through visualizations. I emphasized the importance of confirming the robustness of findings post-imputation and provided an example reporting statement to effectively communicate the validation outcomes.
